{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1TI",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the commandment of God our Savior, and Lord Jesus Christ, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our hope;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To Timothy, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " own son in the faith: Grace, mercy, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " peace, from God our Father and Jesus Christ our Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As I besought thee to abide still at Ephesus, when I went into Macedonia, that thou mightest charge some that they teach no other doctrine,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither give heed to fables and endless genealogies, which minister questions, rather than godly edifying which is in faith; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the end of the commandment is charity out of a pure heart, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a good conscience, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " faith unfeigned:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From which some having swerved, have turned aside to vain jangling;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Desiring to be teachers of the law; understanding neither what they say, nor concerning what they affirm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But we know that the law ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good, if a man useth it lawfully;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing this, that the law is not made for a righteous man, but for the lawless and disobedient, for the ungodly and for sinners, for unholy and profane, for murderers of fathers, and murderers of mothers, for man-slayers,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For lewd persons, for them that defile themselves with mankind, for men-stealers, for liars, for perjured persons, and if there is any other thing that is contrary to sound doctrine,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "According to the glorious gospel of the blessed God, which was committed to my trust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who hath enabled me, for that he counted me faithful, putting me into the ministry;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who was before a blasphemer, and a persecutor, and injurious: but I obtained mercy, because I did ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ignorantly in unbelief:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the grace of our Lord was exceeding abundant with faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a faithful saying, and worthy of all acceptation, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners; of whom I am chief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "However, for this cause I obtained mercy, that in me first Jesus Christ might show forth all long-suffering, for a pattern to them who should hereafter believe on him to life everlasting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now to the King eternal, immortal, invisible, God the only wise, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " honor and glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This charge I commit to thee, son Timothy, according to the prophecies which went before on thee, that thou by them mayest war a good warfare;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Holding faith and a good conscience; which some having put away, concerning faith have made shipwreck:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.1.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.1.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of whom is Hymeneus and Alexander; whom I have delivered to Satan, that they may learn not to blaspheme.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
